From 8ffe13ea241b40157974659e77579fd0d09ee6d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@Averys-Mac-Mini.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:07:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 61/61] win32u, winemac.drv: a child window in another process
 than its parent draws through a remote layer

Edge WebView2 draws its browser into a child window of its host's window,
from its own process (msedgewebview2.exe). winemac gives only top-level
windows a Cocoa window, and a child draws into its top-level window's
surface, which is in the host's process: WebView2's window stayed white.

win32u gives a child window whose parent belongs to another process a
surface of its own, as a top-level window gets; the server already
stops a DC's walk up at a window with a surface, so its own children
draw into it. winemac flushes that surface into a CALayer exported
through a remote CAContext, and tells the top-level window on every
move, resize, show and hide; the top-level window's process hosts it
with a CALayerHost at the child's place. Input already reaches the
child, through the server. The child's cursor is shown by the host's
process, which macOS shows the cursor of: sent as an NSCursor name.
